WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.850
Migration ends on a date.

2
00:00:01.850 --> 00:00:03.200
Certificates don't.

3
00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:05.069
Every one reaches its expiry,

4
00:00:05.069 --> 00:00:09.663
and every authority must keep publishing
a revocation list until then.

5
00:00:09.663 --> 00:00:13.387
So the program watches for trouble
while it can still be fixed:

6
00:00:13.387 --> 00:00:18.134
any certificate close to expiry with no
renewal path, anything issued outside

7
00:00:18.134 --> 00:00:22.662
policy, a trust store holding something
unapproved, a list about to go stale.

8
00:00:22.662 --> 00:00:26.051
The evidence is kept weekly,
because an assessor asks how

9
00:00:26.051 --> 00:00:29.150
long a finding stayed open,
not just whether it's open.

10
00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:30.662
One choice needs care.

11
00:00:30.662 --> 00:00:33.725
Making a valid certificate
a condition of access

12
00:00:33.725 --> 00:00:36.488
turns a failed renewal
into a locked-out user.

13
00:00:36.488 --> 00:00:39.599
So the CISO decides
the grace period first.

14
00:00:39.599 --> 00:00:41.810
Then the old authority can retire.
